<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρῐαπ-ίσκος</span></b> , ὁ, 
			Dim. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρίαπος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dilator</i> or
			<i>suppository</i> for the anus, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.23.72
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				44.14.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>perineal peg,</i> in the Hippocratic bench, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> (or <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i>) ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.26.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>plug</i> for the nose, <i><span class="en">
				Heraclid.
			</span></i> Tar. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.692
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σατύριον</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.126
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				128
			</span></i> (called <i>priapisce,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
